\\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2+0+15 \\\\ -7-10+20 \\\\ 0+0+5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 7{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we can reorder the equations in this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}7{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system using back substitution, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is true, the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id 17592186275384 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186119924 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb5ca50-e9f3-5513-aff1-1ada8c225a42" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent Sets by Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04fd0e5f-aec1-5e47-9884-6914dcdde436" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id 17592186272432} {:answer/id #uuid "53f1398f-c03c-5a8d-aa1c-eb0e6f8cff38" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id 17592186273102} {:answer/id #uuid "ac422526-fbb5-5674-b3b5-76631c070aee" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id 17592186273873} {:answer/id #uuid "ceac787a-b79a-5630-828b-66afa1cf3251" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id 17592186274184} {:answer/id #uuid "fc49f684-7f45-59ee-80e0-cb6b1d9c3f4a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id 1759218